# Line endings: the repository stores LF. Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks out CRLF locally, which is fine for
# source files, but anything that Linux executes must be LF in the working tree too, or the shebang and `set -e` lines break
# ("bad interpreter", "$'\r': command not found") and the CI runner fails.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
# Test fixtures that are compared byte for byte must not change on checkout.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
